### Exercise 5 — Custom handlers, test-first
#
# Run these with the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client, already recommended
# for this project): click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.
#
# These requests CHAIN: look up real reference data, create an empty travel, check rejection,
# add a booking, then submit successfully. No hardcoded UUIDs or dates — the travel uses the
# selected flight's date and currency so the booking fits its period and currency rules.
#
# `cds watch` must be running, with the submitForReview action and handler from Exercise 5.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@auth = alice:

### 1) Grab a real agency ID — SEND FIRST
# @name agency
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/TravelAgencies?$select=ID,name&$top=1
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### 2) Grab a real customer ID
# @name customer
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Customers?$select=ID&$top=1
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### 3) Pick a flight and use its date, price, and currency below
# @name flight
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Flights?$select=ID,date,price,currency_code&$top=1
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### 4) Create an empty travel — expect HTTP 201 Created
# @name emptyTravel
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Review check",
  "beginDate": "{{flight.response.body.$.value[0].date}}",
  "endDate": "{{flight.response.body.$.value[0].date}}",
  "bookingFee": "0.00",
  "currency_code": "{{flight.response.body.$.value[0].currency_code}}",
  "agency_ID": "{{agency.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}",
  "customer_ID": "{{customer.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}"
}

### 5) Submit without bookings — expect HTTP 400 and the "at least one booking" message
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{emptyTravel.response.body.$.ID}})/TravelService.submitForReview
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 6) Add a booking that matches the travel's date and currency — expect HTTP 201 Created
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Bookings
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "travel_ID": "{{emptyTravel.response.body.$.ID}}",
  "flight_ID": "{{flight.response.body.$.value[0].ID}}",
  "flightPrice": "{{flight.response.body.$.value[0].price}}",
  "currency_code": "{{flight.response.body.$.value[0].currency_code}}",
  "bookingDate": "{{flight.response.body.$.value[0].date}}"
}

### 7) Submit the same travel again — expect HTTP 204 No Content
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{emptyTravel.response.body.$.ID}})/TravelService.submitForReview
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 8) Confirm the status moved to InReview (expect "status_code":"P")
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{emptyTravel.response.body.$.ID}})?$select=description,status_code
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
